# ch01 cell plan — "The City Beneath the Dust" (Book of the Soul Pen)
# source scenes: 02 (character), 06 (Kaito/device), 07 (deal), 08 (Afghan airfield),
#                09 (desert city + UFO abduction)
# verse budget total must equal gold chapter (76). pdl: cell|id|title|v_from|v_to|scenes|beat
chapter|ch01|The City Beneath the Dust|solpen|76

cell|01|The Latter Days|1|6|scene_02_ranch_peace.txt;scene_08_afghanistan_battle.txt|In the latter days the nations of the Earth were troubled by wars and rumors of wars. Describe an ancient city in the desert beyond the mountains of Afghanistan, hidden among old roads and forgotten empires, which had endured many kingdoms. Introduce Lucky, a man of great wealth who had seen much of war and trusted few men, cautious of heart, yet desiring to do what was right. Introduce Astra, a woman fierce in spirit, skilled in things seen and unseen, who perceived patterns others overlooked.

cell|02|The Journey|7|12|scene_06_shadow_syndicate.txt;scene_08_afghanistan_battle.txt|There was unrest throughout the region; factions sought power in secret and alliances were formed and broken in secret, while the common people suffered. Lucky and Astra journeyed toward the desert city, having received word that a transaction of unusual importance was soon to take place there. The matter concerned a weapon whose destructive power was beyond that of ordinary arms; many sought either to possess it or to prevent its use. They entered the city under cover of evening while dust blew through the streets, and the city was crowded with travelers, traders, soldiers, refugees, and concealed spies who watched for masters near and far.

cell|03|Kaito the Warrior|13|16|scene_06_shadow_syndicate.txt;scene_07_deal_with_kaito.txt|Introduce Kaito, a warrior who commanded many loyal men, whose reputation was known throughout the region. Some regarded him as a protector, others as a criminal; yet all agreed he was dangerous when opposed. Kaito had also come to the city, for he had learned of the weapon and desired to secure it before it fell into the hands of his enemies. Many paths thus converged upon the same place, though few understood how their destinies were about to become intertwined.

cell|04|The Meeting and Strange Lights|17|30|scene_07_deal_with_kaito.txt;scene_08_afghanistan_battle.txt;scene_09_ufo_abduction.txt|As night fell, Lucky met with informants in a marketplace near the western district; they spoke quietly of shipments, routes, and guarded compounds. One informant warned him, saying there were forces at work greater than the ambitions of warlords and the schemes of governments. Lucky answered that many men speak in riddles when they possess no facts; the informant replied that may God preserve him when the facts arrive. Afterwards Astra observed strange lights moving among the mountains, changing direction suddenly and moving without visible engines, unlike any aircraft known; she reported it to Lucky, and neither understood its meaning. In the following days rumors spread through the city of secret weapons, hidden armies, and visitors from the heavens; most dismissed such reports.

cell|05|The Appointed Day|31|48|scene_08_afghanistan_battle.txt;scene_09_ufo_abduction.txt|The appointed day came. Buyers arrived, sellers arrived, armed men occupied rooftops and alleyways, Kaito's soldiers took their positions, and hidden observers watched from afar; the city grew tense as stillness before a storm. The exchange began; cases were opened, codes verified, payments confirmed. Yet even then there appeared in the heavens above the city a light brighter than any star. Many looked up and pointed in astonishment; others continued their business, believing it some military craft. But the light increased, descended lower, and its shape became visible — unlike any vessel fashioned by the hands of men.

cell|06|The Light and Fear|49|70|scene_08_afghanistan_battle.txt;scene_09_ufo_abduction.txt|Fear fell upon many who beheld it; some fled, others stood frozen, and the soldiers raised their weapons yet no weapon was fired, for all were overcome by confusion. Suddenly the earth shook and a deep, powerful sound filled the air though no source could be seen. Then there descended from the vessel a great beam of blue light, falling upon the place where Lucky, Astra, Kaito, and the weapon stood. Those touched by the light felt their bodies grow weightless; soldiers cried out, merchants fled, crowds scattered in terror. Yet Lucky and Astra could neither run nor resist, for an unseen force held them fast; they began to rise from the ground, and Kaito and certain of his men rose also, and the weapon was lifted with them. Many witnessed these things and trembled, yet none understood what purpose lay behind them.

cell|07|The Ascent|71|76|scene_09_ufo_abduction.txt|As Lucky ascended into the light he looked down upon the city growing smaller beneath him and perceived that the life he had known was ending; for beyond the stars a greater conflict awaited him, not between nations only, but between powers hidden since the foundation of the world. Conclude the chapter with a revelation pointing toward what is to come: Thus ended the days of ignorance, and thus began the journey of the Soul Pen.
